synchronization Issue
---------------------------
Time mapping issue between application and tool is synchronization issue

Selenium handle this using Dynamic Waits

Types
-------------
1.Implicit Wait
-------------------
- Implicit wiat is Global wait as it is applicable for entire script/each element
- Implicit wait you can immediately after driver session 
- If implicit wait is set to 10sec and element found in 6sec then remaining 4sec script will continue with element
- Default timeout for Implicit wait is 0sec
SyntaX:
============
driver.manage().timeouts().implcitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));


2.Explicit Wait
------------------
- Explicit wait it is applicable for single weblement
- Explicit wait we can add based element conditions
			
Two ways to achieve explicit wait in Selenium
--------------------------
1.WebDriverWait class
2.FluentWait class

WebDriverWait extends FluentWait implements Wait(I)

